# Hypnotic Shader for Shadertoy

Here's a mesmerizing hypnotic spiral animation you can paste directly into [Shadertoy](https://www.shadertoy.com/new):

```glsl
void mainImage( out vec4 fragColor, in vec2 fragCoord )
{
    // Normalized coordinates centered at screen middle
    vec2 uv = (fragCoord - 0.5 * iResolution.xy) / iResolution.y;

    float t = iTime;

    // Polar coordinates
    float r = length(uv);
    float a = atan(uv.y, uv.x);

    // Layered distortion
    float distort = sin(r * 10.0 - t * 2.0) * 0.5;
    a += distort;

    // Hypnotic spiral pattern
    float spiral = sin(a * 5.0 + r * 15.0 - t * 3.0);
    float spiral2 = sin(a * 3.0 - r * 10.0 + t * 2.0);
    float spiral3 = cos(a * 7.0 + r * 8.0 - t * 1.5);

    // Pulsating rings
    float rings = sin(r * 20.0 - t * 4.0) * 0.5 + 0.5;

    // Tunnel zoom effect
    float tunnel = 1.0 / (r + 0.1);
    float tunnelPattern = sin(tunnel * 2.0 + a * 2.0 - t * 2.5);

    // Combine patterns
    float pattern = spiral * 0.4 + spiral2 * 0.3 + spiral3 * 0.2 + tunnelPattern * 0.3;

    // Breathing / pulsation
    float pulse = sin(t * 0.8) * 0.15;
    pattern += rings * (0.3 + pulse);

    // Color palette - shifting hues over time
    vec3 col;
    col.r = sin(pattern * 3.0 + t * 0.7) * 0.5 + 0.5;
    col.g = sin(pattern * 3.0 + t * 0.7 + 2.094) * 0.5 + 0.5;  // +2π/3
    col.b = sin(pattern * 3.0 + t * 0.7 + 4.189) * 0.5 + 0.5;  // +4π/3

    // Add bright center glow
    float glow = exp(-r * 3.0) * (sin(t * 2.0) * 0.3 + 0.7);
    col += glow * vec3(0.4, 0.2, 0.6);

    // Concentric wave modulation
    float wave = sin(r * 30.0 - t * 5.0) * exp(-r * 2.0);
    col += wave * vec3(0.1, 0.15, 0.3);

    // Warping rotation layer
    vec2 warpUV = uv * mat2(cos(t*0.3), -sin(t*0.3), sin(t*0.3), cos(t*0.3));
    float warp = sin(warpUV.x * 12.0 + sin(warpUV.y * 8.0 + t)) *
                 cos(warpUV.y * 12.0 + cos(warpUV.x * 8.0 - t));
    col += warp * 0.15 * vec3(0.3, 0.5, 1.0);

    // Vignette for depth
    float vignette = 1.0 - smoothstep(0.3, 1.5, r);
    col *= vignette;

    // Saturation boost
    float gray = dot(col, vec3(0.299, 0.587, 0.114));
    col = mix(vec3(gray), col, 1.4);

    // Contrast enhancement
    col = smoothstep(0.0, 1.0, col);

    fragColor = vec4(col, 1.0);
}
```

## What It Does

- **🌀 Multi-layered spirals** — Three spirals at different frequencies create depth and complexity
- **🔵 Tunnel zoom effect** — A 1/r polar inversion gives the infinite tunnel illusion
- **🎨 Rainbow color cycling** — HSV-like palette smoothly rotates through the spectrum
- **💫 Center glow** — A pulsating bright core draws the eye inward
- **🔄 Warp rotation** — A secondary rotating pattern layer adds organic motion
- **⭕ Concentric rings** — Expanding ring waves reinforce the hypnotic pull
- **🖼️ Vignette** — Dark edges frame the effect and add depth

Just paste it into the Shadertoy editor and hit play! You can tweak any of the multiplier constants to change the speed, density, or color balance.

